[1m[38;5;10msrc/rset.rs[0m[22m — Full Roaring Bitmap implementation with three storage modes:[0m[0m
- **Array mode** (cardinality ≤ 4096): sorted [38;5;10mu16[0m array with binary search for lookups and linear insertion[0m[0m
- **Bitset mode** (4096 < cardinality ≤ 61440): 4096-word bitset covering all 65536 possible values[0m[0m
- **Inverted array mode** (cardinality > 61440): stores items NOT in the set as a sorted array[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Key design decisions matching the C code:[0m[0m
- Empty set encoded as [38;5;10mbuffer[0]=2, buffer[1]=0xFFFF[0m (invalid sorted array state)[0m[0m
- Full set encoded as [38;5;10mbuffer[0]=0[0m[0m[0m
- Automatic conversion between modes at the cutoff points (4096 and 61440)[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mbuffer[0m field made [38;5;10mpub[0m since tests access it directly[0m[0m
- No [38;5;10munsafe[0m code — pure safe Rust throughout[0m[0m
- Uses [38;5;10mwrapping_add[0m for the u16 cardinality counter to handle overflow at the full-set boundary[0m[0m
